      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HOT DIGITY BOOM (3) has the right profile to go on with it after beating TURN BIRD by a long neck at Cairns as a short odds-on favourite. He had already run well at this track when second to COLLEANO in a Class 6 over 1400m, and his distance record gives him a solid base back around 1200m. TURN BIRD (2) is the clear danger, having just missed behind HOT DIGITY BOOM last week after being pipped late, and his proven record at this track and distance keeps him firmly in the winning discussion. ARCTIC BEAR (7) was only just over half a length away in that same Cairns race after beginning slowly, so cleaner manners would bring him closer, though he has not won in three tries at this track and distance. COLLEANO (5) beat HOT DIGITY BOOM over 1400m at this venue last start in Class 6 grade and gets weight relief, making him a genuine place hope with some winning claims if that form carries back to 1200m.",
